  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal, literary word often used in written contexts. The kanji {腐|ふ} (rot) + {心|しん} (heart/mind) vividly conveys the mental strain of intense effort. Common in news articles and business writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～に{腐心|ふしん}する (to devote oneself to ~)\n- {腐心|ふしん}の{末|すえ} (after much deliberation)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {苦心|くしん}: painstaking effort — similar but more common\n- {心|こころ}を{砕|くだ}く: to take great pains — native Japanese equivalent",
